    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3242" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκμήν</span></b> , acc. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκμή</span>, used as Adv., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>as yet, still</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				451
			</span></i> G, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
			</span></i> in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cod.Vat.Gr.</u>
				122
			</span></i>; un-Attic acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Phryn.
				100
			</span></i>, but cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hyp.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				116
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ σκευοφόρα . . ἀκμὴν
			διέβαινε</span> were <i>just</i> crossing the river, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				4.3.26
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				1.13.12
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				4.60
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				7.141
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Antiphil.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Ir.</u>
				p.29
			</span></i> W., <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Matt.</u>
				15.16
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέος ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					25.164
				</span></i>
			; strengthd., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκμὴν ἔτι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					14.4.9
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				15.6.6
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔτι ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sor.
					1.26
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
